      "writtenOn": "2016-02-11T20:24:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "During delete a grant, keystone will revoke tokens that was accessible by this grant. As you can see here: https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/assignment/core.py#L343-L369\n\nSo, this revoke_by_grant will call the _emit_invalidate_grant_token_persistence https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/assignment/core.py#L292\n\nSince, fernet tokens are not persistence, I think this part of code will raise this error. \n\nSo we don\u0027t have to change the status for unauthorized, but handle with this revocation issue related to fernet tokens.",
      "parentUuid": "3a57f1b5_931603f0",
      "revId": "477bf475c158eb1c2ea608d4a51707562168e4f4",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
